From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:47:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 023/106] ASoC: tas2562: drop the regmap defaults, they do not
 match the hardware

The defaults claim values the part does not actually power up with, and
regmap defaults are never written to the chip - they only seed the cache.
So the cache starts out lying, and regmap then drops any write whose value
happens to equal the bogus cached one, believing it redundant.

Seen on a Xiaomi surya: the amp gain mixer control cheerfully reported the
value userspace had set while the gain register on the chip, read back over
i2c, sat at its minimum. The amp was audibly silent, and moving the control
to a different value and back was enough to make the write actually land.
The digital volume was mute for the same reason.

Without defaults the cache is populated from real reads of the part, so it
cannot disagree with the hardware, and writes stop being dropped.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c | 20 +++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
index b3b5f0c62..81f6caff2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
@@ -943,23 +943,21 @@ static const struct regmap_range_cfg tas2562_ranges[] = {
 	},
 };
 
-static const struct reg_default tas2562_reg_defaults[] = {
-	{ TAS2562_PAGE_CTRL, 0x00 },
-	{ TAS2562_SW_RESET, 0x00 },
-	{ TAS2562_PWR_CTRL, 0x0e },
-	{ TAS2562_PB_CFG1, 0x20 },
-	{ TAS2562_TDM_CFG0, 0x09 },
-	{ TAS2562_TDM_CFG1, 0x02 },
-};
-
 static const struct regmap_config tas2562_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_bits = 8,
 	.val_bits = 8,
 
 	.max_register = 254 * 128,
+	/*
+	 * No reg_defaults. They only ever seeded the cache - they are never
+	 * written to the part - and they did not match what the hardware
+	 * actually powers up with, so regmap would drop a write as redundant
+	 * whenever the value happened to equal the bogus default. That is how
+	 * the amp gain silently stayed at its minimum while the mixer control
+	 * happily reported the value userspace had asked for. With no defaults
+	 * the cache is populated from real reads and cannot lie.
+	 */
 	.cache_type = REGCACHE_RBTREE,
-	.reg_defaults = tas2562_reg_defaults,
-	.num_reg_defaults = ARRAY_SIZE(tas2562_reg_defaults),
 	.ranges = tas2562_ranges,
 	.num_ranges = ARRAY_SIZE(tas2562_ranges),
 };
